{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# get_issuelinks_map and get_comment_map are unpaginated\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`JiraDataCenterTransport` builds two whole-project maps with an UNPAGINATED search:\n\n    def get_issuelinks_map(self, project_key):\n        issues = self.search_issues(f\"project = {project_key}\")     # no paging\n    def get_comment_map(self, project_key):\n        issues = self.search_issues(f\"project = {project_key}\")     # no paging\n\n`search_issues` is `(jql, start_at=0, max_results=50)`, so both take the DEFAULT and cover only the\nFIRST 50 issues of any project. Beyond that: issues appear to have NO links (so the differ can emit\nspurious link-creation mutations, and cannot detect removals at all) and comment sync is silently\nincomplete. Neither raises; the pass converges and reports success.\n\nThis is the THIRD known instance of one defect class, and the reason it exists is worth stating: when\n`get_parent_map` had exactly this bug (fixed in change 1105, measured at 20 of 250 parents recovered),\nI patched that ONE METHOD instead of auditing every `search_issues` caller. Two siblings were left\nbehind here, and a third — `fetcher._iter_pages`, which loses 92% of the inbound SNAPSHOT — was found\nlater and is [rebar:deac-4f5a-856a-49bd].\n\n## Approach\n\n**Extract ONE truncation-safe pager and route all three transport callers through it.** Not \"consider\na helper\" — the helper is the fix. Three hand-rolled copies of a paging loop is precisely how the\nsecond and third instances happened, and a fourth caller added later would default to\n`max_results=50` again unless the correct loop is the easiest thing to reach for.\n\nAdd `_paged_search(jql, *, fields=None, page_size=100)` to `JiraDataCenterTransport`, implementing the\nloop already proven in the corrected `get_parent_map`: issue the search at `start_at`, **advance by\n`len(batch)`**, and **terminate only on an EMPTY page**. Driving off the returned rows rather than the\nrequested size is the whole correction — Jira DC silently truncates `maxResults` above\n`jira.search.views.default.max`, so a SHORT page is not proof of exhaustion. Then rewrite\n`get_issuelinks_map`, `get_comment_map` and `get_parent_map` as thin consumers of it.\n\n`get_parent_map` is included deliberately even though it is already correct: leaving it as a fourth\nhand-rolled loop would mean the shared pager exists while the method that motivated it does not use\nit, and the two would drift. Its externally-visible contract is unchanged — including its degradation\ncontract (a failure logs a WARNING and returns `{}` so the inbound pass falls back to its parentless\npath rather than aborting), which is asserted by an existing test that must keep passing.\n\n**Rejected: fixing the two methods in place without a helper.** It is a smaller diff and it is how\nthis ticket came to exist. The structural test from [rebar:bda8-370d-23ad-4e36] catches an UNDECLARED\nmember, not an unpaginated one, so nothing in the tree would stop a fourth instance.\n\n**Relationship to `deac`:** same defect class, different layer, deliberately separate changes. `deac`\nis core `fetcher.py` on the path the live Cloud bridge also uses; this is adapter-local to DC. They\nshare the correction (advance by returned rows, stop on empty) but not the blast radius, and merging\nthem would put a Cloud-affecting change and a DC-only change behind one review.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py` — add `_paged_search`;\n  rewrite `get_issuelinks_map`, `get_comment_map`, `get_parent_map` to use it.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` — held-out regression tests (new module).\n\n## Testing\n\nAgainst a client that serves N issues but caps EVERY page BELOW the requested size — the shape that\ncaught the `get_parent_map` bug, and the shape a hardened DC instance actually presents:\n\n* **happy path** — `get_issuelinks_map` and `get_comment_map` each recover ALL 250 issues from a\n  client capping pages at 20. Both currently recover 50.\n* **the links payload survives paging** — assert link lists from issues on the SECOND and THIRD pages\n  are present, not merely that the map has 250 keys. A pager that returns the right count while\n  dropping payload would pass a count-only assertion.\n* **`get_comment_map` still fetches per-issue comments** for issues beyond the first page, asserted by\n  counting calls, since that method makes an extra call per issue.\n* **empty project** — yields an empty map without raising; an empty project is a normal state.\n* **`get_parent_map` is unchanged in behaviour** — its existing 250-of-250 regression test passes\n  against the refactored implementation, and its degradation contract (WARNING + `{}` on failure)\n  is asserted, since routing it through a shared helper is where that would silently be lost.\n* **structural** — a test asserts NO `search_issues` call in the transport relies on the default\n  `max_results`, so a fourth instance fails the build rather than shipping.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `get_issuelinks_map` and `get_comment_map` each recover ALL 250 issues from a client capping\n      pages at 20, asserted by tests that FAIL against the current code (which recovers 50)\n- [ ] link payloads from issues beyond the first page are present in the returned map, asserted on\n      content and not only on key count\n- [ ] all three whole-project readers route through ONE `_paged_search`, verified by reading the\n      source — no method retains its own `start_at` loop\n- [ ] a structural test asserts no `search_issues` call in the DC transport relies on the default\n      `max_results`, and it is proven to FIRE on a synthetic unpaginated caller\n- [ ] the pager advances by `len(batch)` and terminates only on an EMPTY page, verified by reading\n      the source — a short page must not end the scan\n- [ ] `get_parent_map`'s existing regression test and its degradation contract (WARNING + `{}`) both\n      still pass after it is routed through the shared helper\n- [ ] the full unit suite passes"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785519109633624001,"uuid":"57316a04-7559-4e68-abbb-ed04b65d6ae3"}